{%- comment -%}
  Scarcity line, VARIED PER PRODUCT: the same red line on every product reads
  as fake urgency — a trust and misrepresentation risk.

  Deterministic split on product.id % 10, so a product always shows the same
  state and roughly:
    0–2  (~30%)  red    settings.low_stock_line ("Almost sold out …")
    3–5  (~30%)  amber  "Selling fast — stock is limited"
    6–9  (~40%)  green  "In stock and ready to ship"

  theme.js mirrors EXACTLY this bucket rule in S.scarcityFor() for the quick
  view and the drawer mini-page — change one, change both. settings.
  low_stock_line stays the global off-switch: empty = no line anywhere.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- comment %} id-modulo pseudo-scarcity can read as fake urgency if enabled without
real inventory backing it, which is a trust and compliance risk in some jurisdictions.
settings.scarcity_enabled ships OFF with a warning label so each store can configure
it deliberately. The rule stands: enable only with real inventory gating. {% endcomment -%}
{%- if settings.scarcity_enabled -%}
{%- if settings.low_stock_line != blank -%}
  {%- assign sc_bucket = product.id | modulo: 10 -%}
  {%- if sc_bucket <= 2 -%}
    <p class="pdp-low-stock stmt-sm"><span class="pdp-low-stock__pulse" aria-hidden="true"></span>{{ settings.low_stock_line | escape }}</p>
  {%- elsif sc_bucket <= 5 -%}
    <p class="pdp-low-stock pdp-low-stock--fast stmt-sm"><span class="pdp-low-stock__pulse" aria-hidden="true"></span>{{ 'product.scarcity.fast' | t }}</p>
  {%- else -%}
    <p class="pdp-low-stock pdp-low-stock--stock stmt-sm"><span class="pdp-low-stock__pulse" aria-hidden="true"></span>{{ 'product.scarcity.stock' | t }}</p>
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- endif -%}
